WEBVTT

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.890
<b>Book 1: The Wilderness of Love & Sorrow</b>

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.220
What happened?

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.440
That's a damn shame...

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.820
He's the fifth to have died.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.940
A bigwig from a trading company, 
an electromagnetics professor...

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.800
An onmyoji from the Tsuchimikado clan?

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.800
<b>Episode 2: Confidential File 033, The Treasurer</b>

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:55.380
It looks like all the victims 
were on that stolen roster.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.740
And they were all being provided 
confidential funding by the government...

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.260
These were important individuals,
with big roles to play

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.100
in the country's future.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:09.630
Are you sure you don't mean 
the Tokugawa regime's future?

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.620
I'm not going to dignify 
that with an answer.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.780
What I want to know is how Kuchinawa 
even learned of the roster.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.840
No one except a Nue agent would've known

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.030
where the top secret files 
were being stored.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.480
The assassination plot Hanakaze 
dug up was a diversion.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:32.000
If we can trace the tip back to
 its source, we'll find our traitor.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.120
Understood. I'll get to it.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.270
Hold it.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.930
How's Yukimura doing?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.640
Oh, well, unfortunately...

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.350
Okay!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.310
I did a good job cutting it!

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.780
It saddens me to report that she survived.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.340
It's been four days since her fight.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.320
With her abnormal healing ability, 
she should be up and about again.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.860
It'd be so much easier 
for her if she was dead.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.080
Maybe I should do her the favor...

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.860
If you'll excuse me, sir.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.300
I know.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.080
I've never forgotten... not for a second.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.730
<b>Diary</b>

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.240
Mom, what's that?

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.930
I'm thinking of keeping a diary.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:04.340
So I picked one up when 
I was shopping in town.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.300
A diary?

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.310
<i>On that day... everything was taken from me.</i>

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.750
<i>My mother was murdered before 
she could ever write in her diary.</i>

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.520
<i>Along with my father and my brother.</i>

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.800
<i>Everyone who lived in 
our village was killed.</i>

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.120
Are you digging graves for them?

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.630
Do you want revenge?

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:12.580
Revenge?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:18.730
Right now, there's no way to know who 
killed your friends and family, or why.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:23.800
But if you found them one day, 
would you want to kill them yourself?

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.220
I want revenge.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.480
Then come with me.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.810
<i>We are a secret organization that 
protects our country's head of state,</i>

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.670
<i>Yoshinobu Tokugawa-sama.</i>

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.750
<i>We're called "Nue."</i>

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.000
<i>I'm going to turn you 
into a Nue executioner.</i>

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.390
<i>I'm going to use you to
 make Nue more powerful.</i>

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.600
<i>And you're going to use me 
in order to get your revenge.</i>

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.660
Who the hell are you?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.310
You think you can get away with this?!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.540
I will never forget.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.390
Excuse me!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.080
Thank you.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:39.250
Asahi, I need you to watch the shop.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.060
Huh?! But it's almost time for dinner!

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.040
This town never settles down.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.850
They're always digging for something, 
or patching up the walls...

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.560
It's probably maintenance 
on the artificial Ryumyaku.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:10.990
Without its effects, the electrical 
output drops to around 20.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.970
I didn't ask for a lecture.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.470
<i>It's 1 PM, and we have news 
from the government.</i>

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:21.780
<i>This afternoon, representatives 
from the US, Britain, and France</i>

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.100
<i>out of the secessionist island of Kyushu,</i>

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.370
<i>and the Minister of Foreign Affairs, 
Hidenaga Matsudaira,</i>

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:31.880
<i>met for a four-way conference 
in Matsuyama, Ehime.</i>

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.450
Kyoko-chan!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.880
Yes?

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:37.030
<i>The results were reported immediately 
to Yoshinobu Tokugawa-sama</i>

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.570
I'll take the ginger-fried pork lunch, 
with some croquettes.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.640
And extra rice, please.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.670
I'll have the miso mackerel 
meal, with a boiled egg.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:44.560
<i>and are likely to ensure an advantageous 
bargaining position for our country</i>

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.360
And a small bowl of hijiki if you've got it.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.420
Grilled salmon, meat and 
potato stew, and curry rice.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.560
Sure thing. It's a pleasure 
having you all again.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:51.070
<i>in future trade negotiations 
with the three foreign powers.</i>

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.310
Wow, she doesn't have to 
write any of that down?

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.970
Sorry about that. I'll be right over.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:58.290
<i>In the evening, a group of malcontents causing
 a public nuisance in Miyagi Prefecture</i>

00:08:55.350 --> 00:09:00.120
Can I order the daily special 
from Friday of last week?

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:02.590
<i>were swiftly dealt with by local police,</i>

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.080
That'll depend on if we still 
have the ingredients.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:08.810
<i>with all suspicious 
individuals involved arrested.</i>

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.850
Let me check.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.530
You're the treasurer, then?

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.790
A car is coming.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.810
We're going to escort you to safety.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.860
You had better not think I owe you for that.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.370
I don't.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.980
See, this is exactly why 
you're so damn annoying!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.300
You look after the treasurer.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.540
Understood.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:01.310
Where were you going to take me?

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.220
To a boat.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.410
Going where?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.030
I don't know.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.920
You'll most likely be leaving Tokyo, however.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.330
West or east...

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:14.380
Not that either sounds great.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:18.340
There are riots happening 
all over the place.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.760
Toyama has run out of prison space,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.810
so lately they've been killing 
people instead of arresting them.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.070
The commotion in Yamaguchi has 
been covered up as a pandemic,

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:31.310
but it was actually a crackdown 
on English-funded insurgents.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.020
The bodies were dumped into the sea.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.090
There are a lot of things people 
don't notice living in Tokyo,

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:38.090
and they're probably happier for it.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:39.620
I see.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.740
Then again, maybe it's the same 
no matter where you go.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:47.550
The government doesn't even 
want to admit opposition exists.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.240
That's why they'd never admit that a group

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:55.460
that exists to eliminate anti-establishment 
VIPs like Nue actually exists.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.590
Didn't you know all that before joining Nue?

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:03.930
I did. But they can't keep 
the facade going forever.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:07.240
Anti-regime forces are gaining 
power all over the country.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:10.600
I think people in Tokyo 
realize that, on some level.

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:14.060
So no matter where you go,
 it's all really the same.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:19.030
It's no business of mine who knows what.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.860
It's not? When we're both members of Nue?

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:27.060
We should really hurry.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:33.520
You'll want to take a right at the 
next intersection, and then a left.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:37.340
Another left after that, which 
should take us closest to the harbor.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:43.590
You actually know the full 
layout of the tunnels?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.550
I do, actually.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.690
I also know that you're Sawa Karasumori,

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:52.990
born on December 7th of the year Meiji 46.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:57.640
You were registered as a Nue 
executioner in Meiji 60.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.590
It's something about how my brain works...

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:04.700
I remember everything I see or hear, 
whether I want to or not.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:09.690
All the money and people who operate in 
and around the Tokugawa government...

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.660
It's all in my head.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.880
That's why they call me "the treasurer."

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:20.340
Including incidents where 
the records have been purged?

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.710
And all of the Tokugawa 
government's dirty laundry.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:27.170
Which is why, if Janome gets 
a hold of the intel I have,

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.810
it'll spell doom for the regime.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.100
I won't let that happen.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.520
That's a relief to hear.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.190
<b>Morning Dew Used Bookstore</b>

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.950
Practicing your writing?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:50.680
Tsuki-san!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.890
That looks very nice.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.670
<b>Yuki Yuki Yuki</b>

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.070
What're those?

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:03.040
One of those pills will kill 
someone in ten seconds.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.520
I thought you might have someone 
you'd want to feed them to.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.040
But... Yuki-oneechan is...

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.930
The person who murdered your parents.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.300
Mom?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:38.880
Ready? Do it just like I taught you, okay?

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:02.110
Janome isn't here! I swear!

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.820
We just give him a portion of our profits!

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.240
We have no way of knowing where he could be!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.340
If you don't, then you're of no use to me.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.370
Damn it...

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.190
What's the holdup? Let's get out of here.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.890
We shouldn't stick around long.

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:45.800
Go on ahead. I'll catch up soon.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:51.720
Onee-chan killed my mom and dad...

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:57.860
Don't you think she might be raising 
you so you'll kill her one day?

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:00.600
So that you can get revenge, in other words.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.410
That sounds just like her, really.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:09.930
I tried the other day... but it didn't work.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:18.270
You need to strike where 
you'll do the most damage.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:23.970
And you need to wait... 
until I'm more vulnerable.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:34.030
You're going to make her wish come true, 
and you've got my support.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.320
That's why I want you to have this.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:41.960
Tsuki-san, do you hate Onee-chan?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.540
Not at all. I love her, in fact.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.840
She's stronger—and in more 
danger—than anyone I know.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.980
It makes her hard to leave alone.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:55.050
You don't need to understand. 
Just remember this.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:59.260
It's very hard to live a lie. But...

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.230
What are you doing?

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.030
I need you to answer my questions.

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:11.660
Ten years ago, a mountain town in Aomori 
was slaughtered and burnt down.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:13.980
The Karasumori village, right?

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:15.800
And you're from there...

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:20.540
There are no records of 
what happened anywhere.

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:26.440
They wanted to keep the power of the 
Karasumori clan's blue blood a secret.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:31.200
The only ones who know are me, 
Yoshinobu-sama, Kuzuhara-san,

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.800
Makoto Tsukishiro, and Elena Hanakaze.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.140
And...

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:39.260
And Janome. The man 
who stole my people's power.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.560
Right.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.470
Janome has been able to recreate the 
blue blood's power, although imperfectly.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.870
That's how he creates Changelings.

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:51.510
If I had the detailed records, 
they could lead me to him.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:55.650
The paper trail is long gone, 
but you remember it all, don't you?

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:59.280
I do. But... I can't tell you.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.790
If you don't, I will kill you.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:07.080
If I do, they'll kill my son.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:11.660
Everything about Nue has to 
remain in the shadows...

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.180
That includes me, and everything I know.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.600
If I break that law, it'll mean death.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:23.140
They watch him with his foster family.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.230
Yoshinobu-sama doesn't tolerate treason.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:28.230
He's only five years old!

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.580
He loves watching the clouds pass by!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:33.740
He never gets tired of staring up at the sky!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:38.990
My life means nothing compared to his!

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:46.870
What if I offered to protect both of you?

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:51.230
You'd betray Nue? Just for revenge?

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.710
My entire life is for revenge.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:59.720
Nothing else is of any concern to me.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.760
I can't trust you that easily.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:09.690
For now, if you get on this boat 
with me, I'll consider it.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.450
And if we're able to get my son back,

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:19.860
I'll tell you everything that you don't know.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.510
Everything... that I don't know...

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:34.050
We're less than five minutes 
from the harbor now.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.150
Run!

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.270
I'm out of bolts.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.850
I'll entertain them.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.190
You take care of the big one.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.470
You, who would violate the foundation 
of what makes a man,

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:18.550
dwell now in the blue that surges within!

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:32.220
<i>I will not die in a place like this!</i>

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.160
I do not pity you.

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.440
Nor do I hate you.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:48.170
But for the sake of my 
vengeance, you must die.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.630
<i>Birds live to fly</i>

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.800
<i>In pursuit of flight, they harm others, 
and are hurt themselves</i>

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.720
<i>But once they are in 
the air, there is no light</i>

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:11.430
You can seek vengeance 
on me in the afterlife.

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.920
I won't be long.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.530
I'm going to see Kyoko-san off.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.550
Are you? Those weren't the orders.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:28.740
I think it would be for the best. 
Please notify Kuzuhara-san.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:32.750
How exactly is this going to work, though?

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:36.670
Are you going to paddle with your hands?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.800
Want me to buy you an oar?

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.450
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:43.380
Let me demonstrate.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:54.850
Your son has already died, 
so you can meet him soon.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.780
Even my son?

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:00.570
You'll... pay...

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.960
Why'd you kill her?!
